      "id": "GENUS_POLIOCEPHALUS",
      "name": "Poliocephalus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Two species of Australasian grebes with fine silvery-white streaking on the head, named from the Greek for 'grey head'. They breed in freshwater lakes and are notable for elaborate weed-presentation courtship displays similar to those of Podiceps.",
      "lineage": "Large Grebes",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "POLIOCEPHALUS_POLIOCEPHALUS",
          "name": "Poliocephalus poliocephalus",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Hoary-headed Grebe",
          "lineage": "Large Grebes",
          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The hoary-headed grebe (Poliocephalus poliocephalus) is a member of the grebe family. It breeds in southern parts of Australia; it winters throughout the island of Tasmania. The bird takes its name from the silvery-white streaking on its black head. It is common in Australia, with a population of about 500,000. Its habitat is similar to that of the Australasian grebe.",
          "sourcedFrom": "wikipedia",
          "wikipediaTitle": "Hoary-headed grebe",
